From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P80 builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:21:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Build the virt APEX payload as ext4 for kernels without EROFS

Android 17 builds com.android.virt with a compressed EROFS payload; it is
the only APEX that does. A GSI on a kernel without CONFIG_EROFS_FS (the
Teclast P80's 4.9) cannot mount it: as a bootstrap APEX
(RELEASE_AVF_ENABLE_EARLY_VM) apexd-bootstrap fails and init reboots into
the bootloader ("bootloader,bootstrap-apexd-failed"); without early VM
the APEX stays inactive, framework-virtualization.jar is missing from
BOOTCLASSPATH and ART rejects the boot image's mainline extension.
Use the default ext4 payload, as Android 16 did (99 MB instead of 66 MB).
---
diff --git a/build/apex/Android.bp b/build/apex/Android.bp
--- a/build/apex/Android.bp
+++ b/build/apex/Android.bp
@@ -201,10 +201,7 @@
         default: unset,
     }),
 
-    payload_fs_type: "erofs",
-    erofs: {
-        pcluster_size: 32768,
-    },
+    // Teclast P80 GSI: ext4 as on Android 16, see the commit message.
 }
 
 apex_defaults {
-- 
